-- DECISION: a portal view is the client's row (a tenant table, unlike the operator's `saved_view`),
-- so a shared one never reaches another client. RLS limits every command to the session's client;
-- it can't narrow to the person (sessions carry no user id), so the routes pick a person's own rows,
-- or the shared ones, by `user_id` and `shared`. Views aren't history: changed in place, deleted.
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON portal_view TO cs_runtime;
